| 2026-08-20 | R92 — one occurrence, two branches | **`SessionAudienceBranch (session, branch)`.** The association occasionally delivers a lesson **once instead of twice**: two branches' classes meet together, physically at one of them, for that occurrence only. **Semantics are REPLACEMENT** — no rows means inherit, rows mean *these are the audience's branches* — because an additive reading leaves nobody able to say whether the schedule's own branch still counts. The dialog seeds the override with it already selected, so *combine* is adding the second, said unambiguously. | **PHYSICAL LOCATION AND AUDIENCE BECOME SEPARATE FACTS.** `Session.branch_id` is not overloaded and not written: the class stays at its venue while people come to it from elsewhere, and `GET /sessions/{id}/roster` reports both side by side so nobody infers one from the other. **Scope, never a roster** — branch populations resolved against live Enrollments at read time. | `20260820010000_r92_session_audience_branch` |
