| 2026-08-19 | Every authorization consumer became time-aware, and each date is documented | `studentsTaughtBy` · `teacherBranchIds` · `teachesQuran` · `teacherEventScope` · `assertExamInTeacherScope` · `staffsSession` · R90's candidate conflicts. **Which date each one asks about is a table** in the new `docs/development/teaching-authority.md`, because *default everything to today* was the thing the Owner asked not to do. `readableScope` stays period-blind **deliberately** — it decides which class DEFINITIONS she may read, and hiding a class she taught last term would hide her own history while granting nobody anything. | **`studentsTaughtBy` gained an OCCURRENCE arm**, and it closed a defect: R87 §J opened «إدخال الحفظ» for a one-off cover while the resolver, which knew only about schedules, handed her an empty roster — **rule P inverted**. `teaches_quran`'s occurrence arm was narrowed to the same day, so the marker and the roster ask one question of one date. | None |
