| 2026-08-20 | `verify-staff-picker` closed — and it was hiding a regression | **Two layers, only one obvious.** R91 intentionally replaced the class form's `StaffPicker` with the dated `StaffingPeriods` editor, so an unstaffed class has no person select until a row is added — and the harness matched the add control with `=== 'إضافة إسناد'` while the shared `Button` renders the add variant as **`＋إضافة إسناد`**. Exact equality never matched, the row was never added, and the probe reported an empty picker on a working control. One form probe settled it: type `class`, `ClassSection`, legend «المؤطّرات وفتراتهن», button `＋إضافة إسناد`. | **Then it earned its keep.** With the row finally added, check 5 failed on a **real regression**: `StaffingPeriods` rendered bare names, so moving a class onto it had silently dropped R90's *marked before the choice* half — the chips after selection still worked, which is what made the loss invisible. `markedLabel` and `Warnings` are now exported from `StaffPicker` and shared, guarded by a source assertion that the periods editor keeps no private copy. **A harness that cannot reach its control reports the product broken and stops testing it.** | None |
| 2026-08-19 | Three harness defects, and what each was really saying | **A raw `prisma.create` fixture has no occurrences** — materialization lives in the service, and every per-date assertion came back empty against a schedule that had none. **`/dashboard/teacher` is not a route**: «الصفحة غير موجودة» has no menu, and the harness read that as a hidden entry for somebody whose roster and marker were both correct. **One refresh cookie, one consumer** for the third time: `tokenFor` rotates the cookie it uses, so loading the app with the same one afterwards renders a logged-out shell. | Recorded in `testing.md` beside the traps they join. The general lesson is the one that keeps recurring: **check what the page actually rendered before believing an absence**, and a fixture must exercise the mechanism under test rather than simulate its output. | None |
