| 2026-08-19 | Sending is a decision, taken after the save | **The change is saved first and unconditionally**; a separate authorization-checked request decides delivery. A flag on the write would let a failed notice roll back a change that succeeded, and the person has not decided at the moment the form submits. **Declining calls nothing** — it is the absence of a request, not a request that sends zero. Authorization is the event's own edit assertion, exported rather than re-implemented. | `ConfirmDialog` gained an optional `cancelLabel`: «بدون إشعار» is a decision, not a cancellation of one. The client names the KIND of change and never the recipients — a body attempting to is **refused** by the `.strict()` schema. | See above. |
| 2026-08-19 | A personal calendar, and the public one unchanged | **`GET /calendar` was a visibility-tier read being used as a personal one** — a beneficiary saw every public session in the platform. `GET /me/calendar` narrows the SAME projection at read time: her enrolments' sessions and the events addressed to a scope she belongs to; for a مؤطرة, what she is assigned to. **No per-user rows**, so a moved enrolment is right on the next read rather than needing a backfill. | Verified by asking as three different people — 6 occurrences for the concerned beneficiary, 4 for the unrelated one, 58 on the public calendar that still shows both. The negative halves are what make the positive ones mean anything. | See above. |
