| 2026-08-18 | Regression from 65823c6 — dialogs rendered as page content | **One declaration, most of the platform.** The single-scroll fix added `display: flex` to `.dialog` unconditionally, and a native `<dialog>` is hidden by exactly one UA rule — `dialog:not([open]) { display: none }` — which author styles outrank at every specificity. Every screen that keeps its add/edit dialog mounted (a native dialog must be in the DOM to be openable) rendered it permanently, in flow, under the table; the calendar's day dialog is `--wide`, which is the block that appeared on the public calendar. | **The affected/unaffected split was the diagnosis**: the surviving pages mount their dialog conditionally, and both sets are now swept. `display` is scoped to `[open]`, the closed rule is stated explicitly in the author sheet, and the single-scroll architecture is untouched — 15 pages verified for closed · open · close · reopen · page-flow · scroll ownership. | None |
