| 2026-08-17 | UX/IA pass 2 | **Seventeen items from a second Owner correction pass — every one fixed in a shared component rather than on the screen that reported it.** **(1) A missing translation key ships as user-facing text.** `t()` returns its own argument on a miss, so `نقاط الامتحانات` rendered a table headed `admin.schedules.title`, `admin.exams.date`, `admin.exams.audience` — and the **same three keys had been wrong on `/teacher/exams` first**, so the defect propagated by being copied, which is the shape a missing guard always produces. `i18n/resolves.test.ts` now resolves **every literal `t()`/`tList()` key in the application** against the catalogue; it found exactly those six and nothing else. It states its own blind spot — computed keys belong to the registry guards that enumerate their values. **(2) Unsaved form work survived a stray click.** A backdrop click threw away everything typed, with no warning. `Dialog` gained `dismissible`; `FormDialog` makes the decision from a `dirty` prop and asks with the **shared** `ConfirmDialog`. All five form dialogs report it through one pure comparison — `isDirty` takes **both sides**, because these dialogs write their fields in an effect *after* first render and a captured baseline would report *dirty* the instant an edit dialog was populated. **`dirty` defaults to `false`**, so omitting it is silent; a guard fails any form that does. **(3) Row actions did not look clickable.** `DataTable` rendered them `ghost` — no border, no background — in a cell full of text. They are the shared `Button` now (`secondary`, `danger` for destructive), so **the last hand-written class list on the platform is gone** and the atomic guard's allowlist has one entry. **(4) The page header wasted its width.** `space-between` plus a flex item's default `min-width: auto` pushed single words onto their own line with empty space beside them — reported on three pages, fixed once in `.admin__head`. **(5) The sidebar could not reach its own last entries.** It scrolls itself now, with `overscroll-behavior: contain` so reaching its end does not silently start scrolling the page. Three CSS declarations, no JavaScript. **(6) `المستويات` promised behaviour R66 removed** — *"creating a Level also creates «المجموعة 1»"* has been false since the group became optional. **(7) Two columns left `المستويات` and one left each of `مقرر الحفظ`/`مواد المستوى`**: each counted a relationship another page owns. `enrollment_count` stays, because a Level's enrolled مستفيدات are a fact about the Level itself. **(8) `إتمام المستفيدات` left `مقرر الحفظ`** — the engine, BR-11 and the `complete: null` third state are untouched on their endpoint; a presentation moved off a curriculum page. **(9) `مواد المستوى` edits in a `FormDialog`** — it was the last in-page editor, architecturally the odd one out, and is now the same `FormDialog` + `MultiSelectField` shape `مقرر الحفظ` uses for the identical concept. **(10) `المواد` shows each Subject's linked Levels**, named rather than counted: a paired Subject cannot be deleted, and a number tells an administrator they are blocked while the names tell them what to unpair. **(11) `تفاصيل المستوى` became `المستفيدات`** on `حلقات المواد` — the row is a circle, and its roster is what the table is for. **`GET /admin/teaching-groups/{id}/members` completes a collection whose `POST` and `DELETE` were specified in R43 and whose `GET` was missing — which is exactly why the `DELETE` had no caller at all.** Candidates come from BR-22's own `unassigned` list, so the Administrative Group is not read and the two placements stay independent (§4.4c). **(12) The enrolment edit dialog offers branch and circles.** `updateEnrollmentPlacement` has accepted `branchId` all along; Level stays absent because BR-21 makes `(student, level)` the enrolment itself. **(13) The exam scale question was already answered, twice.** §7 calls `SystemSetting` *runtime-editable* and names the grading scale in it; R14 puts both values there and nowhere else — **and they were seeded by §15.1 and reachable by nothing in the product**, the same gap `legal.consent_text_version` had before R42. They join the writable allow-list, integer-validated (§20 rule 3). **A per-exam maximum mark was NOT added: R58 refused it in terms** — *"a second answer to what `grading.display_scale` already owns"*. Per-level overrides are specified in §7 and remain unbuilt; recorded, not half-implemented. **(14) Found while testing, not in scope:** `reference-data.http.integration.test.ts` deleted users without clearing the `Trash` rows they authored — `Trash.deleted_by` is `ON DELETE RESTRICT` (R59), so the suite's own cleanup broke the moment it soft-deleted anything. **Three of my own new tests were wrong before the code was:** two assumed a student free to join a circle when §4.4c had correctly refused her a second seat in one Subject, and one asserted a Level↔Subject pairing the fixtures never made. **(15) Seven rules documented (T–Z)** and three guards **restated rather than deleted** — they had pinned an accordion, a row action's URL and a removed badge, none of which was the property they existed for. | **New:** `i18n/resolves.test.ts` · `lib/form-dirty.ts` · `Dialog dismissible` · `FormDialog dirty` + shared discard confirmation · `.row-action` · `GET /admin/teaching-groups/{id}/members` · `CircleRosterDialog` · `SubjectsDialog` · `subjectWithLevelsDto` · grading scale in `WRITABLE_SETTINGS` + `SettingDto.kind` · `--measure-lede` · `.chip`. **Removed:** the last hand-written button classes · `CompletionView` · the in-page level-subjects editor · 3 redundant columns. **Docs:** `ux-architecture.md` rules T–Z + guard register · CLAUDE.md. **No schema, no migration, no SRS edit, no authorization change.** 1129 backend + 474 frontend tests, 15 CI guards, lint · typecheck · build clean | None |
| 2026-08-17 | UX/IA pass | **A platform-wide UX consistency and information-architecture correction — and the audit's finding decided its size: the atomic foundation already existed, so this is a migration rather than a construction.** `Button`, `DataTable`, `Pagination`, the five §14.4 states, `levelLabel`, `MultiSelectField`, `FormDialog` and `ConfirmDialog` were all already the platform's one implementation of their concept. **The defects were drift at the edges**, and every one of them had appeared before on another screen. **(1) Five pages gated their own data behind a dropdown.** `نقاط الامتحانات` opened on «اختاري امتحانًا» with an empty page; `مقرر الحفظ`, `مواد المستوى`, `حلقات المواد` and `/teacher/quran` were accordions or selectors over data nobody could see. All five are now **title → description → primary action → filters → table → pagination → row actions**, and the deep links (`?exam=`, `?level=`, `?student=`, `?subject=`) survive **as focus rather than as gates**. R69 had already fixed this once on `حلقات المواد`; the recurrence is why the rule is now written down and guarded. **(2) There were TWO button systems.** `.button` / `.button.primary` lived in `status-pages.css` with its own class name, its own padding and none of `ghost`/`danger`/`add`, across **ten call sites** on the registration, status and profile pages — so the platform had two answers to *what does a button look like* and the status pages got the one nobody maintained. All ten now render `ButtonLink`; the CSS block is deleted. A further five files hand-wrote `btn btn--*`, including a `<span>` styled as a disabled button, which is now `<Button disabled>` — the element that actually carries the role and the state. **(3) The `＋` convention lived in a TRANSLATION STRING for exactly one screen**, so `تسجيل مستفيدة` carried it and `إضافة مجموعة` did not. It is now `<Button variant="add">`, which emits the glyph so a caller cannot forget it — applied at every create call site. **(4) Three copies of the Level label, and two selectors rendering bare names.** §4.4b makes Level names non-unique across Categories, so a bare name does not identify one. `approvals.tsx` held a third copy of the `{Category} — {Level}` format; the calendar's Level filter and the groups page rendered `level.name` while joining Category names was **one lookup away in the payload they already had** — `withCategoryNames` does it. **(5) Grade entry no longer labels a person.** The `النتيجة` column read «ناجحة»/«راسبة». **`Grade.passed`, `manual_pass_fail_override` and BR-12 are untouched in the model and still decide retakes and progression** — what is removed is a *verdict about a مستفيدة on a grade sheet*. The manual override is still surfaced, because it is provenance rather than a verdict. **(6) §5.3's `/dashboard/student/grades` finally exists.** It has been in §14.1 since R62 and **nothing rendered it**: a مؤطرة could publish a grade and the student it was about had no way to see it — the **sixth** instance of this project's recurring shape, a complete capability with no reach. `GET /students/me/grades` selects `status: 'published'` **in the query**, so a draft is absent rather than hidden, and the projection carries no verdict, no basis points and no draft state. **(7) Placement is discoverable in one workflow without merging two concepts.** The enrolment form offers optional circles alongside the optional group — as **two existing server calls in order**, keyed on the **Level alone**, because a circle is `(Subject, Level)` and reloading it when the group changed would assert a dependency §4.4c does not have. A failed seat does not roll back the enrolment: they are independent placements, and discarding the one the administrator definitely wanted to protect one they merely also wanted would be the wrong trade. **(8) «إنهاء التسجيل» was audited and the implementation was already correct** — soft delete, circle seats released, R59 Trash entry, grades and Quran logs retained. What was missing was copy distinguishing it from *changing a placement* and stating what survives; `ConfirmDialog` gained **one** optional `details` slot rather than one screen growing its own confirmation. **(9) The «66» was one string**: `groupHint` read *«…صحيح بعد المراجعة 66»* — an SRS revision number on a form hint. A sweep of every catalogue **value** for `§`, `TD-`, `BR-n`, `Rnn` and `مراجعة n` found no other. **(10) The مؤطرة's access was already granted; her labels misled.** «حصصي» and «المحتوى التعليمي» named what the back office calls «الجدولة» and «مكتبة المحتوى» — one platform, two vocabularies. Her paths, her roles and her §4.4c scope are unchanged, and `/admin/content` is **deliberately not** offered: that would be an authorization change dressed as a rename. Her sidebar is now grouped like the back office's. **(11) `الإدارة` is reordered** to الفئات → المستويات → المواد → **مواد المستوى → مقرر الحفظ**, which is §14.1's own dependency order for the first four. **(12) Two defects found while wiring, neither in scope:** `fetchMyCoverage` never sent `X-Active-Child-ID`, so a parent-only account got a `400` on `/dashboard/student/quran` and one holding both roles saw **its own** progress instead of the child's — the server was right throughout, the client never named the child; and `admin.users.create` survived as an **orphaned catalogue entry** after its button was removed, shipping in the bundle for a future screen to pick up. **Nineteen lettered rules are now documented and guarded**, and three guards that pinned the *accordion's implementation* were **restated as the property** rather than deleted — one asserted the absence of `<LevelSelect`, which the redesign uses as a **filter**, so the rule's fulfilment was being read as its violation. | **New:** `ui/searchable-select.tsx` (one choice from many, options visible on open) · `Button variant="add"` + `ADD_GLYPH` · `withCategoryNames` · `GET /admin/teaching-groups` (flat, filtered, TD-10-paginated) · `GET /students/me/grades` · `/dashboard/student/grades`. **Deleted:** `.button` CSS system · `CreateDialog` + 6 orphaned strings · the `النتيجة` column · one revision-number leak. **Converted to data-first:** exam grades · circles · Quran curriculum · level subjects · teacher Quran. **Docs:** `docs/development/ux-architecture.md` (19 rules A–S + the guard register) · audit · CLAUDE.md *Platform UX & Atomic Design Rules* · documentation-policy routing · frontend architecture. **No schema, no migration, no authorization change, no SRS edit.** 1119 backend + 462 frontend tests, 15 CI guards, lint + typecheck + build clean; live-verified 14/15 then 10/10 on the published-grade path, plus 30 served-bundle assertions | None |
| 2026-08-14 | R66 bug class | **The group-less-enrolment NULL-relation defect, closed as a class rather than one more instance.** A Prisma **relation filter never matches a NULL relation**, so every query resolving *is this student enrolled in this Level* by requiring `administrativeGroup: { … }` silently excluded students enrolled directly in an unsubdivided Level — **silently** being the problem: no error, no empty state, just a person missing from a list she belongs on. It had been introduced **five times across three slices**, and **twice the `select` was migrated to `Enrollment.branch_id` while the `where` beside it was left behind**. **P0 — consent re-evaluation.** `enqueueConsentReevaluationForStudent`'s `entire_level` arm skipped a group-less student entirely, so BR-2/§4.9's gate never re-ran for her sessions and a withdrawal of consent could leave a recording published. Reproduced live before and after: **1 session requeued for both shapes now, 0 for a genuinely unenrolled student**. **P1 — circle candidates.** `listUnassignedStudents` required a live group **and nested its branch filter inside that relation**, so a group-less student was never offered — the server accepted her into a circle while the screen could not show her. Branch scoping now reads **`Enrollment.branch_id`** (R66), which is the referent that exists for both shapes. **P1 — private library content.** Three sites in `library.service.ts` — a student's own Levels, a parent's children's Levels, and branch ordering — hid a group-less student's own Level from her and from her parent. A stale pre-R66 docstring naming the `Enrollment → AdministrativeGroup.branch_id` chain was corrected with them. **A guard for the class, not the instances.** `group-less-enrollment.test.ts` scans enrolment queries and refuses any that requires a live group, while **accepting the ones that are legitimately about a particular group** (they name `administrativeGroupId`, including object shorthand). **It was proven to fail on a reintroduced defect and pass when restored**, and it states its own blind spot: a nested `level.enrollments.some` — where the P0 lived — is not a call it can see, so the semantic tests carry that case. **All 14 enrolment queries were classified rather than blanket-rewritten**; the genuinely group-specific ones are untouched. **One further site found and deliberately left:** `calendar.service.ts:676` (prefill only — no wrong data, nothing hidden that authorization allows), recorded in the guard's allowlist with its reason and scoped out by the Owner. | 5 predicates in 3 services + 1 stale docstring; `group-less-enrollment.test.ts` (2 guard assertions) and `group-less-enrollment.integration.test.ts` (13 semantic tests). **No schema, no SRS, no new concept, no authorization change.** 1104 backend + 438 frontend tests, 15 CI guards; live-verified 13/13 | None |
| 2026-08-14 | M4c | **`LevelSurah` management and BR-11 level completion — the last M4 slice.** **`LevelSurah` is the Quran-side curriculum join** (R43 keeps it so while the Quran is a Subject *for scheduling only*), and it had **no service, route or screen** and zero rows. It now sits **beside `LevelSubject`, in the same file with the same authorization**: **Super Admin writes, Admin reads** (R26's reference-versus-operational split). Assignment **revives** a removed row rather than failing on the unfiltered unique pair, and **removing a Surah leaves the logged progress untouched** — §4.5 records against `(student, surah)` and BR-13 derives from the logs, so the syllabus decides what BR-11 *requires*, never what a مستفيدة has *recited*. **BR-11 reads the existing engine and computes no new percentage.** Completion is *configured Surahs x the coverage §4.5 already derives*, through the **same `recalculateFor`** every mutation and read uses — so a completion figure and a dashboard figure cannot disagree, and R10's self-heal comes with it. **Three states, not two:** a Level with **no configured Surahs** reports `complete: null`. Coverage of an empty syllabus is vacuously total, and reporting that as completion would let a Level nobody has configured mark every مستفيدة finished. **The final-exam clause is structurally absent, and that is faithful rather than a shortcut.** Nothing in the model marks an exam as a Level's final one — `Exam` carries `round`, which §4.6 defines as *an optional non-restricting selector used solely for sorting*, explicitly not a semantic marker. So BR-11's own *if no final exam is configured, coverage alone suffices* is **the only reachable branch**, and it is reported as `final_exam_configured: false` rather than silently omitted, so the day a marker exists the gap is visible. **No marker was invented.** **The screen shows its data**: every Level with its syllabus and its enrolled مستفيدات' completion, expanding per Level (completion resolves coverage per student per Surah, so eager loading would be a request storm). It reuses the shared Level label, the atomic multi-select for the 114, `FormDialog`, `Badge` and the empty states. **`GET /admin/quran-surahs` exposes the seeded lookup** rather than hardcoding 114 names — §4.5 calls that table the definitive denominator, and a client-side copy would be a second source of truth for reference data. | `listLevelSurahs` / `assignSurahToLevel` / `unassignSurahFromLevel` / `listQuranSurahs` in `reference-data.service.ts`; `levelCompletion` in `quran.service.ts` over the exported `recalculateFor`; 5 routes; `/admin/level-surahs` (Super Admin **by placement**, R61); 18 catalogue strings; 10 integration tests. **No schema, no migration, no SRS change.** 1091 backend + 438 frontend tests, 15 CI guards; live-verified 14/14 | None |
| 2026-08-14 | E2E verification | **The whole chain walked against the running stack — 30 assertions — and it found a silent R66 break.** `مستفيدة → مستوى → مقر → مجموعة → مادة → حلقة → امتحان → نقاط` verified end to end through the HTTP API. **The defect: a student enrolled directly in an unsubdivided Level could join NO teaching circle at all.** `studentBranchInLevel` had its `select` updated for R66 — its comment even says the branch *"exists for an ungrouped student too"* — while its `where` still required `administrativeGroup: { deletedAt: null }`. **A relation filter does not match a NULL relation**, so a group-less enrolment read as *not enrolled in this level* and was refused `409 NOT_ENROLLED_IN_LEVEL`. R66 and §4.4c were broken together, silently, and no unit test could see it because every fixture had a group. Fixed with the predicate `levelsForStudent` already states correctly — *the enrolment is live, and IF it has a group that group is live too* — plus **two regression tests**, one for the fix and one asserting the guard it stood in for still refuses a genuinely unenrolled student. **Everything else held.** The whole-Level audience resolved to the Level's students **at the exam's branch** and correctly excluded the same Level at another branch (R66); the group exam resolved to its group alone; **circle membership had no effect on exam eligibility in either direction** — a student with no circle sat the whole-Level exam, and one with a circle did not sit the other group's; BR-7 initialised two absent-zeros; 15/20 stored as **7500 bp**; publish → amend-returns-to-draft → **republish** reported as such; and a مؤطرة read only the sheet for the group she staffs while one staffing nothing was refused. **Administrative Group ≠ Teaching Circle, demonstrated:** a student in Group 1 and a group-less student joined the *same* circle. | One-line predicate fix in `teaching-group.service.ts` + 2 integration tests. **No schema, no SRS, no model change.** 1081 backend