e code, Category, Level and branch belong to the dashboard's identity block and widening `/me` is how a session probe becomes a profile endpoint. Links to soft-deleted children are excluded — `resolveActingStudent` refuses them on the next request, so listing one renders an option that always answers `404`. **`/dashboard/parent` is gone** (R62.9): a parent's home is `/dashboard/student`, the path now resolves to `not-found` rather than `screen-pending`, and the difference is the point — `screen-pending` promises a page that is coming. **The active child now persists in `sessionStorage`**, because choosing a child will also switch the active role and switching navigates by full page load: the selection was destroyed by the action that made it. The staleness argument that kept it in memory is answered by reconciliation against `/me` on every load, not abandoned. **`composeArabicName` extracted to `lib/person-name.ts`** — R62 had rewritten `${first} ${last}` inline at three more sites, which is the same reasoning the schema gives for why a *client* must not compose a name, applied to two servers. **11 HTTP integration tests for the child-application endpoints, which had none**: auth, the per-child consent refusal, `mine` never leaking `internal_note`, teacher `403` on both admin routes, `ALREADY_DECIDED` on a second decision, duplicate proposals carrying reference code + linked family — and the one no service test can reach, **submit → approve → `/me` names the child**, which is the only assertion that proves the flow terminates somewhere a parent can use. | `/me` `approved_child_links` is now `[{id, display_name}]` (client type, `use-navigation`, `linkedChildren` adapter); `RegistrationResult.child_id` → `child_application_ids`; `ROLE_HOMES` parent → `/dashboard/student`; `ActiveChildProvider` gains `activeChild` + `sessionStorage`; user-journeys J1/J2, `frontend.md`, `identity-and-access.md` corrected | None |
