ctually changed, not what was requested**. A `404`/`409` is read as *someone else decided this first* and reloads, because the administrator needs to see it is no longer theirs to decide. The Type filter goes to the **server**, unlike the Branches search which narrows already-fetched rows: a queue is paginated over the full set, so filtering client-side would hide matches on later pages — and changing it resets to page 1, which is otherwise an empty table on a queue that has matches. **Verified live against the running stack, not assumed:** seeded a real pending parent+child bundle, confirmed the response shape matches the adapter field for field, both item types present; `?type=` narrows to exactly one kind each way; a reason-less reject returns `VALIDATION_FAILED`; approving returned **`records_updated: 2`** (parent + child, atomically); re-approving returned **409**. Fixture rows removed afterwards. **10 new component tests** (135 frontend, was 125) | §14.3's `ApprovalCard` built; `Badge` now shared; `ConfirmDialog` generalised without a behaviour change for existing callers | None |
