## The assessment builder was unreachable for مؤطِّرات — rule P, instance seven — 2026-09-04

The Owner named **three** authorised author roles: Super Admin, Admin and
**Teacher**. `assessment.service` implemented all three from the first commit —
a مؤطِّرة authors within her own teaching through `assertExamInTeacherScope`, and
a test already proved that one outside scope is refused. **She had no route.**
`/admin/assessments` carries `roles: STAFF`, and `STAFF` on this platform is
`['admin', 'super_admin']`; no teacher node existed.

So the authority was real, the screen was built, and one of its three intended
users could not reach any of it — a complete capability with no reach, which is
this project's most repeated defect and the reason rule P is written down.

**`/teacher/assessments` renders the same component**, exactly as
`/teacher/exams` reuses the grade sheet (R70.1). One implementation, two
chromes; what differs is what the server will accept, not what the screen can
do. The two menu guards were **restated, not relaxed** — the node list and the
R106 flat order both name it now, with the reason recorded beside the
`/teacher/quran` precedent, which was the same defect in the same shape.

**One stale guard reason corrected while here.** `scheduling-exam.test.tsx`
justified having no online field on the sitting form with *«when the mode
arrives it needs … a shape nobody has decided»*. R124 decided it. The property
still holds and the assertion is unchanged; only its reason was false, and a
guard whose stated reason is wrong is one the next person misreads or deletes.

Frontend: typecheck, lint, build, **1004/1004**.

## Two more planning lines were stale, and one apparent TD-3 gap was my own error — 2026-09-04

**Visibility transitions are complete**, not partial. The line said *«general
visibility editing and the friendly stale-link page remain»*; both are built.
Editing goes through `VisibilityField` on the content dialog and
`PATCH /content/{id}`, and the transition is not a flag flip: it **copies to the
target bucket, verifies size and SHA-256 against the source, commits under an
optimistic version guard and only then retires the old key** — a failed copy is
discarded and the original left untouched. `/content-unavailable` is routed and
rendered.

**Teacher scope is complete.** `teacher-scope.ts` does not exist; `GroupTeacher`
survives only in two historical schema comments. Every staff-scope question
